{"name":"Marmot","hex":"#928475","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marmot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several large ground-dwelling rodents of the genera Marmota and Cynomys in the squirrel family."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marmot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marmot","blocks":[{"text":"Marmots are large ground squirrels in the genus Marmota, with 15 species living in Asia, Europe, and North America. These herbivores are active during the summer, when they can often be found in groups, but are not seen during the winter, when they hibernate underground. They are the heaviest and largest members of the squirrel family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/071_Wild_marmot_at_Grand_Muveran_Nature_Reserve_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-071_Wild_marmot_at_Grand_Muveran_Nature_Reserve_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marmot","wikidata":"Q131567"},{"title":"Marmot (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Marmot is an American outdoor recreation clothing and sporting goods company. The company, headquartered in Rohnert Park, California, was founded by David Huntley, Eric Reynolds, and Tom Boyce."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marmot_(company)","wikidata":"Q1902277"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Marmot1.jpg/500px-Marmot1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Marmot1.jpg/1280px-Marmot1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Marmot1.jpg/500px-Marmot1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marmot in its natural habitat","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarmot1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https